 determine the distance between any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with side length 6 units, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry of a Regular Hexagon:**\n   A regular hexagon can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles. Each side of the hexagon is the same as the side length of these equilateral triangles, which is 6 units.\n\n2. **Identify the Distance Between Parallel Sides:**\n   The distance between any pair of parallel sides in a regular hexagon is equal to the height of one of these equilateral triangles. We need to find the height of an equilateral triangle with side length 6 units.\n\n3. **Calculate the Height of an Equilateral Triangle:**\n   The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) can be found using the formula:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n   \\]\n   For our hexagon, the side length \\( s \\) is 6 units. Plugging in the value, we get:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   The distance between any pair of parallel sides of the regular hexagon is \\( 3\\sqrt{3} \\) units.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:95"}
